Z||000020||JohnnyK||10-21-2001||10:41 PM||||Speaking of.. I have a 110v wire feed solar welder. It says good for up to 1/4. My question is, I guess I can't weld two solid 1"-2" round bars together? (Like, in a T form for instance). Or can I? I don't have gas at the moment (it's meant for gas, but I'm using flux). I really want an arc welder though.||||reg||1
Z||000021||artherd||10-21-2001||11:03 PM||||mmmm TIG welder......<P>PS: if you ever find a girl who knows what a TIG welder is, and wants one herself, I suggest you marry her asap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Alas, I missed my chance...<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000022||fierospeeder||10-21-2001||11:23 PM||||ive heard that also,  theres a chance that your contact can melt? into your eye.<P>in highschool, i had machine shop, and we had experts come in and showed us an hour video of all eye injuries, ALL eye injuries.  nothing but eye.  ||||reg||1
Z||000023||maryjane||10-21-2001||11:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnnyK:<BR><B>Speaking of.. I have a 110v wire feed solar welder. It says good for up to 1/4. My question is, I guess I can't weld two solid 1"-2" round bars together? (Like, in a T form for instance). Or can I? I don't have gas at the moment (it's meant for gas, but I'm using flux). I really want an arc welder though.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>You can weld it with your machine,but won't be able to get a lot of penetration with a small machine. Something like that, you want to take a grinder, put a bevel around the end of one piece, and make several passes. Clean it good between passes. Still won't be as strong as a big machine can do (weld should be nearly as strong or stronger than the material itself), but will probably do ok for stuff aroud an auto shop, if you are pretty experienced. Just remember that the weld that is sticking up above the material does little to provide strength. Ya need penetration, but don't use a setting so hi that it just melts the wire, or rod if you're using a stick welder. I used to weld well heads on in the oilfield, have more problems with thinner stuff.Always trying to weld too hot + can't see well anymore.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000024||Spektrum-87GT||10-22-2001||05:17 PM||||wow, im not suprised you know what the ronald regan is... i AM suprised you called it the CVN 76! its coming along great, near finished from what I understand. I'm working on CVN78 right now(yeah, CVN 77 has barely begun  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) which is odd for me... its like years down the road  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by maryjane:<BR><B>Spek, I just realized where you work. How's the Ronald R,(CVN 76) comin along? Looks like a big sucker.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000025||AkursedX||10-22-2001||06:52 PM||||Ok, here is some of my welding work.  This was just prelimnary and there was more welding done, but you will get the point on how it can be beneficial to Fieros.<P>To orient you, this picture is at the back passenger side wheel-well.  The metal piece that I am welding in is to replace the rusted out section of the frame-rail that was once there.  It's right near the trunk area.  Notice how much of my trunk is rusted out.  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P8280005.JPG"> <P>Now this picture is of the completed side, with the new frame-rail welded in, new sheet metal to replace the trunk area, and it is all painted.  Looks like a brand new car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P9220026.JPG"> <P>I did this to the other side as well.  So the rear end and the entire battery tray area is basically as good as new.  I will probably do this to the front end after winter as well.<P>Note:  this is my 87GT, not the '88 in the sig  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
